# MTQ UiX - AI Assistant Rules

You are working with the **MTQ UiX** admin panel: a strict-TypeScript, Feature-Sliced Design (FSD)
React application built on the CoreUI component library. It uses Vite for build/dev, React Router 7
for hash-based routing, React Context + hooks for state, and Storybook for component documentation.

## Tech stack

- React 19 + TypeScript 6 (strict), ES2022
- Vite 8, React Router 7, Sass/SCSS
- CoreUI 5 (consumed as `@mtq/design-system`)
- Storybook 10, ESLint 9 + Prettier + `eslint-plugin-boundaries`

## Architecture (FSD)

Imports flow only downward:

```
app → pages → widgets → features → entities → shared
```

| Layer | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `src/app` | entry, providers, router, global styles |
| `src/pages` | one component per route; composition only, no business logic |
| `src/widgets` | self-contained page blocks |
| `src/features` | user-facing state/actions (`model/`, `ui/`) |
| `src/entities` | domain data, types, selectors (no side effects) |
| `src/shared` | api client, config, utils, base UI helpers |

Rules:

- Never import upward or across slices on the same layer.
- Every slice exposes a single public `index.ts`; no deep imports.
- The design system lives in `packages/design-system` (`@mtq/design-system`); app code never
  imports `@coreui/*` directly and never re-implements a primitive.

## TypeScript conventions

- `strict: true`. No `any` (use `unknown` + narrowing). No enums (`as const` objects).
- `import type { … }` for type-only imports (`verbatimModuleSyntax` is on).
- Prefer `type` for unions, `interface` for extendable shapes.
- Explicit return types on exported functions/components.

## Component & state conventions

- One component per file, named after the file; co-locate `.stories.tsx` for UI.
- Functional components only.
- Local UI state: `useState`/`useReducer`. Global UI state: context in `features/*` (e.g.
  `features/sidebar`). No Redux. Server state belongs in `shared/api` (TanStack Query later).

## Styling

- All visual values are design tokens (`var(--cui-*)`, `var(--color-brand-*)`). No hardcoded
  colors/fonts/radii/spacing.
- Use `@mtq/design-system` for all primitives/icons/charts; use CoreUI utility classes for layout.
- Conditional classes via `cn()` from `@/shared`; token lookup via `cssVar()` from `@/shared`.

## Commands

```bash
npm start              # dev server (http://localhost:3000)
npm run build          # production build → build/
npm run lint           # ESLint (TS, React, prettier, FSD boundaries)
npx tsc --noEmit       # strict type check
npm run storybook      # Storybook (http://localhost:6006)
```

Before finishing any change, ensure `npm run lint` and `npx tsc --noEmit` pass.
